<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Larova · Arabic strings.

  A translation, not a source: never fix wording here. Fix the English in values/strings.xml and
  re-translate. See docs/localization.md.

  **A model draft, not yet read by a native speaker.** docs/localization.md §5 names the three
  parts that must not ship on a machine draft — the help bar and contact sheet, the two view names,
  and the six templates. Arabic needs a second kind of check besides the wording: it is the only
  right-to-left language in the set, so the Latin fragments left in it on purpose (Larova, PIN,
  http://) have to be read *in the running layout*, not in an editor, where bidirectional
  reordering can put a slash or a colon somewhere it does not belong.

  Arabic has six plural forms (zero / one / two / few / many / other) and every <plurals> below
  carries all six.
-->
